es with that in mind  on september 20th many people came  forward with experiences  that resembled this kind of scam one  user named it's pack boy  claimed that he had been scammed by rack  and posted a ton of screenshots that  appeared to show a discussion about the  alleged scheme  between himself and another 2k community  member called  range or eric lim the discussions are  about returns on money that was  allegedly being lended to iraq  who also use the name ben it's packboy  said that he trusted  range because he was a member of the  australian new zealand 2k community  what we see in screenshots is that range  appeared to be the one coordinating the  money  in the receipts he asked for money up  front promising quick returns  after a couple such transactions the  pressure for bigger money  escalates its pack boy screenshots  include receipts of him sending  three thousand dollars to an account  owned by someone named calvin bai  but with step back rack 2k as the  subject  a later message from range appears to  show him  pressuring people who were lending money  not to back out on future  opportunities after sending the money  the receipts show a long series of  promises  excuses and delays that led nowhere he  refers to rack as  ben and he was seemingly using that name  throughout this entire situation  as this screenshot from its pack boy  shows another user squoogs  alleged that not only did range scam him  he did it after sqoogs  actually sheltered range in his home  when he was kicked out by his family  even worse squoog estimates that the  amount scammed from the community  was actually upwards of three hundred  thousand dollars  but others have come forward with  accusations against iraq  including one who wasn't even involved  in 2k  so after the accusations rak dropped off  the face of the planet 2k  community members who were looking for  him found a facebook post with a comment  from someone called danny saleh it  accused rack  of withholding money 